  "id": "eval.2026-07-28-eval-170417.rag-ingestion-retrieval",
  "title": "RAG ingestion, retrieval, and rebuild",
  "description": "# RAG ingestion, retrieval, and rebuild\n\nA left-to-right system map showing scheduled/change-driven source arrival with ACLs, normalization and content-hash classification, versioned chunking, reliable embedding, and publication gated on a consistent vector/fragment/keyword version. The lower flow follows a user question through parallel hybrid retrieval, fusion and reranking, permission filtering, evidence-gated grounded generation with citations, and a feedback loop that reprioritizes ingestion. The rebuild lane creates a new index generation in the background, checks consistency, and atomically promotes it while preserving rollback; decision branches represent bypass, quarantine/dead-letter recovery, partial-write repair, and low-confidence refusal paths.",
  "mode": "diagram",
